// TEST: category model-drift
// Regression fixture for #1244: proves the self-hosted `c_emitter.vow`/
// `ir_printer.vow` fix actually feeds ESBMC a real double constant for a
// bare float literal operand, not the raw i64 bit pattern reinterpreted as a
// decimal integer. A wrong constant here inflates `0.25` into an enormous
// value, which breaks the `result <= 2.0` postcondition instead of just
// differing cosmetically in dumped IR text.
//
// The two bounds on `x` are split into separate `requires:` clauses rather
// than joined with `&&` in one clause: a pre-existing, unrelated vacuity-
// detection gap in the verifier's `--error-label`/`vow_reach` reachability
// probe misclassifies a single `&&`-conjoined pair of float comparisons as
// unreachable (reproduces on today's `main` with plain f64 parameters, no
// literals involved) — this fixture is not about that gap.
module FloatLiteralContract

fn add_small(x: f64) -> f64 vow {
  requires: x >= 0.0,
  requires: x <= 1.0,
  ensures: result <= 2.0
} {
    x + 0.25
}
